    "answerSummary": "### 1. Conceptual Breakdown (Plain English)\n**What it is:** Annotate test methods with @Feature(\"User Authentication\"), @Story(\"Password Reset\"), and @Severity(SeverityLevel.\n**Why it matters in QA:** Understanding this concept enables QA engineers to bridge the gap between business specifications and technical verification, eliminating guesswork and test flakiness.\n\n### 2. Deep-Dive Technical Explanation\nAnnotate test methods with @Feature(\"User Authentication\"), @Story(\"Password Reset\"), and @Severity(SeverityLevel.CRITICAL). Inside test steps or afterEach failure hooks, attach visual artifacts using Allure.addAttachment(\"Failure Screenshot\", new ByteArrayInputStream(screenshotBytes)). Run \"allure generate allure-results --clean -o allure-report\" to build the interactive HTML report.\n\n### 3. Step-by-Step Practical Application Guide\n• **Step 1: Identify Preconditions & Scope:** Clarify the exact system boundary, inputs, and expected environmental states before executing.\n• **Step 2: Construct Deterministic Assertions:** Avoid relying on arbitrary delays; instead, assert against explicit system state transitions and verifiable outcomes.\n• **Step 3: Isolate Environmental Variables:** Ensure test data is cleanly provisioned and cleaned up so parallel or subsequent runs remain independent.\n\n### 4. Key Terminology for QA Engineers\n• **Deterministic Testing:** A testing approach where a given input always produces the exact same observable outcome without intermittent or random failures.\n• **Flakiness (Flaky Test):** A test that intermittently passes and fails on identical application builds without any code changes, usually caused by timing race conditions or shared mutable state.\n• **Quality Gate:** An automated checkpoint in the CI/CD pipeline that blocks flawed builds from progressing to staging or production.",
    "codeSnippet": "// Allure Annotations in TestNG / JUnit\n@Test\n@Feature(\"Payment Gateway\")\n@Story(\"Stripe 3DS Verification\")\n@Severity(SeverityLevel.BLOCKER)\npublic void testStripeThreeDS() {\n  Allure.step(\"Initiate payment with 3DS card\", () -> { ... });\n}",
